+## Failed session setup
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model-response hooks run, and cleanup must tolerate setup having completed only partially ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
+Decision for #94: `afterSession` runs even when setup fails, using its existing session argument with no new started flag; deployers must track their own allocations and release only resources they acquired, since cleanup does not imply that setup succeeded or that a model turn started.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
